Luxon: echo PhotonPing probes

The client sends a connectionless 13-byte probe (12 x 0x7d followed by a marker) to a candidate
server before it opens a session and expects it echoed verbatim. It carries no ENet header, so
without this it fails parse_packet and the client's region probe times out; the client then
abandons the match with a network error although the name server answered.

Recovered from the kf-staging NAS build (/root/kf-photon-build, image kickflight/photon:pingfix,
2026-10-28), where it was an uncommitted change on top of Luxon 5401810.

diff --git a/src/enet/enet_server.cpp b/src/enet/enet_server.cpp
index dcaee39..dbdf768 100644
--- a/src/enet/enet_server.cpp
+++ b/src/enet/enet_server.cpp
@@ -89,6 +89,17 @@ void EnetServer::service_self() {
             break;
         }
 
+        // PhotonPing: a connectionless 13-byte probe (12 x 0x7d followed by a marker) that the
+        // client sends to a candidate server before it opens a session, and which it expects
+        // echoed verbatim. It has no ENet header, so without this it fails parse_packet below and
+        // the client's region probe times out — it then abandons the match with a network error
+        // even though the name server answered perfectly.
+        if (r == 13 && datagram[0] == 0x7d && datagram[11] == 0x7d) {
+            sock_.send_to(buf.data(), r, from);
+            ENET_METRIC_ADD(enet.pings_in, 1);
+            continue;
+        }
+
         // Parse header to find challenge/peer id, etc.
         EnetPacketHeader hdr;
         std::vector<EnetCommand> cmds;
